Features
********

   • Turn any YouTube playlist or channel URL into an org-mode table
     that refreshes with a single command.
   • Two update commands: buffer-wide (‘youtube-gt-update-all’) or just
     the single playlist at point (‘youtube-gt-update-at-point’).
   • Columns 2 and 3 are yours: use them for ‘watched’, ‘to-review’,
     ratings, priorities, running commentary -- whatever fits your
     workflow.  Annotations survive every update.
   • A row you annotated stays in the table even after the video leaves
     the current view -- removed from the playlist, or excluded by a
     later change to ‘:offset’ / ‘:min-length’.  Its index becomes ‘NA’
     so it stands out, but its annotations are never silently lost.
     Unannotated rows that fall out of view drop away, so the table
     never grows into noise.
   • Per-directive filters: ‘:offset=N’ (skip the first N videos) and
     ‘:min-length=N’ (keep only videos of at least N minutes).  Combine
     either way; malformed forms are rejected before any API call.
   • Works uniformly on individual playlists and on whole channels
     (‘@handle’ URLs are resolved to the channel's uploads playlist).


